  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hu">Hu</ref> 4.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ buton þara oðer hæbbe, nele him mon nænne team geþafian.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et nisi alterutrum habeat, nolumus ei permittere cenningam aliquam.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn-2">Absque uero utro (id est alterius eorum testimonio) nulla ei attestacio indulgeatur (id est: liceat ei trahere aliquem ad tutelam, quod ab eo habuit).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ buton þara oðer hæbbe, nele him mon nænne team geþafian.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And unless he has the cognisance of one or other of these, he shall not be permitted to vouch to warranty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und ausser wenn er deren eine hat, weigere man, ihm einen Gewährzug zu gestatten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And unless he has one of these, let him be refused permission to vouch to warranty.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">‘he’ was inserted in B in the 16th century.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
